Signed-off-by: Hans de Goede <hdegoede@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Andy Shevchenko <andriy.shevchenko@linux.intel.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the use of a single sparse keymap that combines both button and switch inputs, which can lead to incorrect reporting of available inputs to userspace. Specifically, the system may incorrectly indicate the presence of switches when they are not available, or vice versa, causing inconsistencies in user experience and functionality. The split into separate keymaps allows for more accurate representation of the hardware capabilities.

